    "text": "WHEAT: Projected U.S. 1997/98 ending stocks are down 23 million bushels from last month because of smaller spring wheat production. The projected price range is up 15 cents on the bottom and 5 cents on the top to $3.20 to $3.70 per bushel. Projected 1997/98 global production is little changed from last month as larger crops in Russia, Eastern Europe, and Mexico largely offset smaller prospective output in the United States, the EU, Syria, and Canada. Larger global imports and exports are mainly due to increased intra-EU trade (trade between countries in the EU). EU imports and exports also are revised for 1996/97 and 1995/96.\n\n<ts></ts>",
